===
title: About
---
Last Signal is Story A: a complete, small visual novel made from Yarn, JSONC screens and CC0 prototype assets.
The colored rectangles stand in for Mara, Ivo and the lighthouse. The quiet tones demonstrate music and ambience.
Use Continue or Space for dialogue, 1–2 for choices, Tab/Enter for buttons. Save at the first display of a scene after its fades settle.
-> Return to the menu
    <<jump Start>>
===
title: Arrival
---
<<checkpoint scene.arrival>>
<<hide cg 0>>
<<hide overlay 0>>
<<move left 0.25 0.5 1 1 0>>
<<move right 0.75 0.5 1 1 0>>
<<voice none 0>>
<<effect none 0>>
<<background bg.day>>
<<show left actor.alice 500>>
<<show right actor.bob 500>>
<<music audio.music 500>>
<<ambience audio.ambience 500>>
Mara: The ferry leaves at dawn. If the beacon stays dark, they will pass us.
Ivo: The old receiver still has power. The antenna on the roof does not.
Mara: My sister promised to listen tonight. I promised there would be something to hear.
Ivo: Then we have one battery and two bad ideas.
<<show background bg.night 800>>
Mara: We could repair the receiver down here, or carry the battery up to the antenna.
<<jump Decision>>
